{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Patch set 2 pushed to 3261 (`6a1783c1f4a`) — verify green, reply posted\n\n`make verify` RC=0: 20497 passed / 27 skipped (default tier, 1:21:17), 203 passed / 3 skipped\n(integration tier, 5:26). 0 FAILED or ERROR lines.\n\nThis is the run that confirms the regression fix. The previous attempt failed\n`test_completion_precheck_threads_one_collector_through_pass_and_sidecar` because two of my own\npatch-set-2 changes interacted: making `_refuse_open_sunset_marker` unconditional routed every\nprecheck test through the marker scan, and the fail-closed guard in `_marker_lines` was matching\ngit's stderr text. `git grep` reports a missing directory and a non-repository with the **same\nexit status 128** and different prose, so the placeholder root `/code` raised instead of\nreturning no markers.\n\nFixed structurally rather than by widening the string match: a `_has_repository` helper runs\n`git -C <root> rev-parse --git-dir`, and the scan consults it only on an unexpected status. No\nrepository reachable → empty answer; repository present but the scan failed → still raises. A\nreworded or localized git message cannot turn a failed scan into a silent pass.\n\nThe regression also exposed a bad test fake. `test_a_failed_scan_raises_instead_of_passing_the_close`\nmonkeypatched `subprocess.run` to return 128 for *every* call, so once the fix added the\n`rev-parse` probe that same fake would have driven the guard down its benign branch and the test\nwould have silently stopped exercising the raising path. Its fake now answers by argv —\n`rev-parse` → 0, `grep` → 128 — which models a real repository whose grep failed.\n\nAwaiting `LLM-Review +1` and `Verified +1` on patch set 2.\n"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793713872729303499,"uuid":"16a05996-ac89-40e2-b2f4-1b24078ff537"}